{"tool_name":"multik","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"multik","home":"https://github.com/siyao-liu/MultiK","license":"MIT","summary":"MultiK is a data-driven tool that objectively assesses the optimal number(s) of clusters based on the concept of consensus clustering via a multi-resolution perspective.","addition_date":"2022-01-12T21:13:07.711873Z","last_update_date":"2022-01-12T21:13:07.714864Z","tool_type":["Library"],"accessibility":"Open access","biotools_curie":"biotools:multik","cost":"Free of charge","credit":[{"email":"cperou@med.unc.edu","name":"Charles M. Perou","orcidid":"https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9827-2247","typeEntity":"Person"},{"email":"marron@unc.edu","name":"J. S. Marron","typeEntity":"Person"},{"name":"Aatish Thennavan"},{"name":"Joseph P. Garay"},{"name":"Siyao Liu"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Aggregation","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3436"},{"term":"Clustering","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3432"},{"term":"Essential dynamics","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3891"}]}],"name":"MultiK","operating_system":["Linux","Mac","Windows"],"owner":"Jennifer","publication":[{"doi":"10.1186/S13059-021-02445-5","metadata":{"abstract":"\u00a9 2021, The Author(s).Single-cell RNA sequencing (scRNA-seq) provides new opportunities to characterize cell populations, typically accomplished through some type of clustering analysis. Estimation of the optimal cluster number (K) is a crucial step but often ignored. Our approach improves most current scRNA-seq cluster methods by providing an objective estimation of the number of groups using a multi-resolution perspective. MultiK is a tool for objective selection of insightful Ks and achieves high robustness through a consensus clustering approach. We demonstrate that MultiK identifies reproducible groups in scRNA-seq data, thus providing an objective means to estimating the number of possible groups or cell-type populations present.","authors":[{"name":"Garay J.P."},{"name":"Liu S."},{"name":"Marron J.S."},{"name":"Perou C.M."},{"name":"Thennavan A."}],"date":"2021-12-01T00:00:00Z","journal":"Genome Biology","title":"MultiK: an automated tool to determine optimal cluster numbers in single-cell RNA sequencing data"},"pmcid":"PMC8375188","pmid":"34412669"}],"topic":[{"term":"Electron microscopy","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0611"},{"term":"Mapping","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0102"},{"term":"RNA","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0099"},{"term":"RNA-Seq","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3170"},{"term":"Transcriptomics","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3308"}],"validated":1},"bioschemas":{"name":"MultiK","home":"https://bio.tools/multik","license":"MIT","summary":"MultiK is a data-driven tool that objectively assesses the optimal number(s) of clusters based on the concept of consensus clustering via a multi-resolution perspective.","tool_type":"sc:SoftwareApplication"},"oeb":{"metrics":[{"@id":"https://openebench.bsc.es/monitor/metrics/biotools:multik/lib/github.com","@license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/","@nmsp":"biotools","@type":"metrics","deprecated":true,"distribution":{"binaries":{"freeness":null,"registration":null},"packages":null,"source_packages":true,"sourcecode":{"free":true,"interpreted":true,"license":true,"public":true,"readme":true,"repository":{"anonymous":true,"online":true}}},"project":{"build":{},"deployment":{},"license":{"open_source":true,"osi":true},"publications":[{"entries":[{"cit_count":25,"citations":[{"count":1,"year":"2026"},{"count":2,"year":"2021"},{"count":3,"year":"2022"},{"count":4,"year":"2023"},{"count":6,"year":"2024"},{"count":9,"year":"2025"}],"doi":"10.1186/s13059-021-02445-5","pmcid":"PMC8375188","pmid":"34412669","ref_count":55,"refs":[{"count":1,"year":"2005"},{"count":1,"year":"2016"},{"count":2,"year":"2002"},{"count":2,"year":"2010"},{"count":2,"year":"2011"},{"count":